cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use snai-int8 or its measurement series, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "snai-int8: integer training of small transformer language models"
authors:
  - given-names: Sebastian
    family-names: Woratsch
    alias: komakeule57-maker
repository-code: "https://github.com/komakeule57-maker/snai-int8"
url: "https://github.com/komakeule57-maker/snai-int8"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  A research engine for training small transformer language models almost
  entirely in integer arithmetic: int8 weights and activations, an integer
  backward pass and gradient accumulation, and 8-bit Adam moments. With
  SNAI_I8_REST=sr it trains without any per-weight floating-point state.
  The engine is written in Nim with CPU (OpenMP), CUDA and OpenCL backends
  that are bit-identical to the CPU reference. The repository also contains
  the research log: measurement series, each with a pre-registered
  criterion, recipe, raw values and verdict.
keywords:
  - int8 training
  - integer-only training
  - quantized training
  - stochastic rounding
  - small language models
  - transformer
  - Nim
